{title: Round and Round Jericho}
{subtitle: Joshua 6:1–20}
{key: F}
{tempo: 120}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [–] | [F] [C] | [F] [C] | [F] [C] |
| [F] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Jericho was shut up tight
No [Bb]one out and no [F]one in
Walls so high and gates so strong
How [Bb]could Israel ev[C]er win
But [Bb]the LORD said to Joshua
See, I give [C]this town to you
March around [Bb]it, trust in me
That is all [C]you have to do
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
March, march, round and round
[C]Ram's horn trum[Bb]pets make a sound
[F]One, two, three, four, five, six, sev[C]en
Shout to the [Bb]LORD, the God of heav[C]en
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Day [F]one, day two, round we go
Feet go stam[Bb]ping, nice and slow
[F]Not a word and not a cheer
Only trum[Bb]pets loud and clear
[C]Day three, day [Bb]four, five and six
[F]Once around [C]and back to camp
Quiet mouths [Bb]and listening ears
Stamp, stamp, stamp, [C]stamp
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
March, march, [F]round and [C]round
Ram's horn [Bb]trumpets make a [F]sound
One, two, three, four, five, six, [C]seven
Shout to [Bb]the LORD, the God of [C]heaven
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]On day seven, up at dawn
Round and [Bb]round and round and [F]on
Seven times they marched around
Then the [Bb]trumpets, what a [C]sound
Shout! For the LORD has given you the city
Every[F]body, take a breath
Shout! For the LORD has given you the city
And the wall fell down [Bb]flat
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Rahab's house was safe [C]inside
With the red cord at [Bb]the wall
God keeps [F]every prom[C]ise made
God is stronger than it all
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C]March, march, round [Bb]and round
Ram's horn [F]trumpets make a sound
One, two, [C]three, four, five, six, [Bb]seven
Shout to the [C]LORD, the [F]God of heaven
{end_of_chorus}

